{"type":"text","timestamp":1772831824475,"sessionID":"ses_33afe223affe3uN9rDLMVQJuCQ","part":{"id":"prt_cc502bf620011aGmIJ1FAGb7I6","sessionID":"ses_33afe223affe3uN9rDLMVQJuCQ","messageID":"msg_cc502922e001F5UmLjqmqW1Ljc","type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"plan\": \"Based on codebase analysis, the server already has authentication via SERVER_API_KEY and SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY environment variables (config.go:32,37). The backend checks auth via checkAPIAuth() function (api.go:63-82). The feature requires a frontend modal overlay.\\n\\n**Frontend Changes (Go Templates):**\\n1. Add modal overlay HTML/CSS to index.html (server/templates/index.html)\\n2. Add JavaScript to check localStorage for stored API key on page load\\n3. If no key stored or invalid, show modal and block main content\\n4. Add key validation endpoint or use existing /api/clients auth check\\n5. Store valid key in localStorage when submitted\\n6. Add logout/clear key button in header that clears localStorage and shows modal\\n\\n**Backend Changes (Go):**\\n1. Create /api/auth/validate endpoint that checks key against SERVER_API_KEY\\n2. Ensure all existing API endpoints continue to require auth (already implemented)\\n\\n**Implementation Steps:**\\n1. Add auth validation endpoint in api.go - POST /api/auth/validate accepting {key} and returning {valid: true/false}\\n2. Modify index.html to include modal overlay with key input field\\n3. Add JavaScript to:\\n   - Check localStorage for 'apiKey' on load\\n   - Validate key via /api/auth/validate\\n   - Show modal if invalid or missing\\n   - Store key in localStorage on successful validation\\n   - Handle logout button click to clear localStorage and show modal\\n4. Add CSS for modal overlay (centered, semi-transparent backdrop, input field, submit button)\\n5. Ensure all content is hidden/shown based on authentication state\"\n}\n```","time":{"start":1772831824474,"end":1772831824474}}}
